Hi there nimble users and developers,

I have been working on a nimble version of the Rota et al. 2016 co-occurrence model. I have six iterations of the model that represent differing hypotheses regarding the system of interest I want to rank using marginalized WAIC.

As a first step prior to attempting marginalized WAIC I have been trying and failing to get conditional WAIC for the simplest of the six models.

Following Chapter 7.2, page 82 of the nimble guide it says " To enable WAIC for the first approach, the argument enableWAIC = TRUE must be supplied to configureMCMC" and  "The WAIC (as well as the pWAIC and lppd values) is extracted by the member method mcmc$getWAIC".

However attempting this, I am returned with:

"Class method definition for method getWAIC()
function ()
{
    if (is.null(".basePtr"))
        stop("Object for calling this function is NULL (may have been cleared)")
    ans <- .Call("CALL_MCMC_getWAIC", .basePtr)
    ans <- ans[[1]]
    ans
}
<environment: 0x00000203f4cb11d8>"

Thus, I moved to attempt the posthoc approach of:

calculateWAIC(posteriorSamplesMatrix, Rmodel)

but was initially returned with:
Error in mcmc_checkWAICmonitors_conditional(model = model, monitors = sampledNodes,  :
  To calculate WAIC in NIMBLE, all parameters of data nodes in the model must be monitored.
  Currently, the following parameters are not monitored: z.

