Dear Josh,

Thanks for posting the question.

A "method" refers to a function of an object of some class.  So, to use a method, you would call it as you would call a function, with opening and closing parentheses.  In this case, please try "mcmc$getWAIC()".  As for regular R functions, if you just enter the method name without parentheses, the output will be the code for the method.

I realize it can be frustrating to be pointed to documentation when you have already made an effort to work through it, but I do want to mention this is shown at the end of help(WAIC), which is suggested from the User Manual (chapter 7.7 on p. 82 is what I think you meant).

I hope that gets you going!  Good luck with it.

Perry

